  "name": "Voxel Noise: Discretizing the Continuum",
  "title": "Noise Carved into Blocks",
  "lookup_name": "Noise_Voxel",
  "description": "A fixed Perlin field becomes a sampled occupancy decision. A cased 24-cubed model controls a five-times-larger volume with matching cells. A live screen compares one horizontal score slice with the exact occupied/empty mask; the dark orb keeps its independent pulse. Threshold changes classification, CELL selects a sample and screen layer, SEED changes the field, and CUT changes only the model view. Connected occupied cells do not establish a walkable route.",
